Experiment:
Modify the SoftFoldSkip module to include a linear layer that takes the input tensor as input and outputs the skip weight. The skip weight will then be used to scale the output of the SoftFold layer before it's added to the original input, creating an input-dependent skip connection. Specifically, the Agent class will be modified as follows:

class Agent(nn.Module):
    def __init__(self, envs):
        super().__init__()
        def create_mlp(output_dim):
            return nn.Sequential(
                layer_init(nn.Linear(np.array(envs.single_observation_space.shape).prod(), 64)),
                nn.Tanh(),
                SoftFoldSkip(64),
                layer_init(nn.Linear(64, 64)),
                nn.Tanh(),
                SoftFoldSkip(64),
                layer_init(nn.Linear(64, output_dim), std=1.0 if output_dim == 1 else 0.01),
            )

        self.critic = create_mlp(1)
        self.actor = create_mlp(envs.single_action_space.n)

class SoftFoldSkip(nn.Module):
    def __init__(self, width):
        super().__init__()
        self.softfold = SoftFold(width)
        self.skip_weight_layer = layer_init(nn.Linear(width, 1)) # Input-dependent skip weight

    def forward(self, x):
        folded = self.softfold(x)
        skip_weight = torch.sigmoid(self.skip_weight_layer(x)) # Sigmoid to keep weights between 0 and 1
        return x + skip_weight * folded

Key metrics: episodic return, training stability (variance of the episodic return), and the distribution of the learned skip weights across different inputs.
